Hello,

On "random" moments the firmware crashes. After checking the kernel log, 
it seems to be crashing after limiting the TX power.
It crashes more often on battery than plugged in. Sometimes every 5 
minutes. It's much worse on public places with lots of clients, for 
example eduroam (university wifi) in a library.

I used to have kernel panics but I think that is fixed when upgrading 
the kernel.

Device: Dell XPS 13 9370 on kernel 4.19.13
Chip: QCA6174
Firmware: WLAN.RM.4.4.1-00079-QCARMSWPZ-1

[102810.299786] wlp2s0: Limiting TX power to 11 dBm as advertised by ...
[104289.349299] ath10k_pci 0000:02:00.0: firmware crashed! (guid 
e8a86ca7-c883-4430-b3bf-282e43c4b962)

dmesg log attached (I don't really know which parts are needed, I 
